---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PartyQuiz from '../components/PartyQuiz.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

/*
 * The pricing page.
 *
 * Richard's call: Jen quotes every job herself rather than publishing fixed
 * numbers. So this page doesn't list prices — it answers the price *question*,
 * which is most of what the search intent actually is.
 *
 * Worth being straight about the tradeoff: SEO-PLAN.md §4 recommends
 * publishing real starting numbers, because no competitor in the county does
 * and it filters out tyre-kickers before they reach her inbox. A quote form
 * captures the same searches but converts a little worse and lets some
 * unqualified enquiries through.
 *
 * What makes this page still work: it answers "what drives the price", "is
 * there a minimum" and "how fast do I hear back" — the three things a nervous
 * buyer is actually asking when they type "how much does a dessert table
 * cost". Competitors answer none of them. Add real starting numbers later and
 * this page gets materially stronger.
 */

const title = 'Party Pricing & Packages | West Palm Beach';
const description =
  'Real answers on what a party costs in West Palm Beach — no $5,000 minimums. Tell Jen about your event and she quotes it herself, usually within a day.';

const faqSchema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Is there a minimum spend?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'No. Jen takes small parties that larger event companies turn down. There is no minimum package you have to grow into.',
        },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'What affects the price of a party?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'Guest count, how much of it is hand-made versus assembled, the size and detail of any hand-painted signage, whether desserts are included, and whether Jen sets up and breaks down on the day.',
        },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'How do I get a price?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'Fill in the short form with your event type, guest count, date and budget range. Jen prices every job herself and usually replies within a day or two.',
        },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Why do you ask for my budget?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'So Jen can tell you quickly and honestly what is possible at that number, instead of designing something you were never going to book. A range is enough.',
        },
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base {title} {description} schema={faqSchema}>
  <section class="section intro">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
      <h1>What it costs.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Jen prices every party herself, because no two are the same job. What
        she will tell you up front is what actually moves the number — and that
        there's no minimum you have to hit before she'll take the booking.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--navy">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>No $5,000 minimum.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        A lot of event companies around West Palm Beach won't return a call
        under five figures. Jen will take the small backyard first birthday and
        the forty-person shower, and she'll put the same hands on both. That's
        not being cheap — it's being available.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What moves the price</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Five things, in roughly the order they matter.
      </p>

      <ol class="drivers">
        <li>
          <h3>How many people</h3>
          <p>
            Forty guests is more dessert, more favors and a bigger table than
            fifteen. This is usually the single biggest factor.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>How much is made by hand</h3>
          <p>
            Individually iced cookies and a hand-lettered banner take real
            hours. Simpler dessert and printed signage cost less. Jen will tell
            you where the hand-made detail is worth it and where it isn't.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Signage size and detail</h3>
          <p>
            A small painted tabletop sign and a six-foot painted backdrop are
            different jobs. Wording length and artwork complexity both count.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Whether desserts are included</h3>
          <p>
            Some people want the whole table. Some want the banner and styling
            and are handling food themselves. Both are fine.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Setup, breakdown and travel</h3>
          <p>
            Dropping off is one price. Arriving early, styling the room and
            coming back to break it down is another. Distance matters too —
            she's based in {site.location.city} and travels across Palm Beach
            County.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Straight answers</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <article>
          <h3>Why don't you list prices?</h3>
          <p>
            Because a number on a page is either so vague it's useless or so
            specific it's wrong for your party. Jen would rather look at what
            you're actually planning and give you a real figure she'll stand
            behind.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Why do you ask my budget?</h3>
          <p>
            So she can be honest fast. If what you're picturing doesn't fit the
            number, she'll say so and tell you what would — rather than
            designing something beautiful you were never going to book. A range
            is plenty.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>How fast will I hear back?</h3>
          <p>
            Usually within a day or two. Jen reads every enquiry herself — there
            is no office and no assistant between you and her.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Can I book just one thing?</h3>
          <p>
            Yes. Plenty of people order only a banner, or only a tray of
            cookies. You don't have to book a whole party to work with her.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="quote" class="section">
    <div class="wrap band">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Get Your Price</p>
        <h2>Tell Jen about your party.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Four taps and your email — what you're celebrating, how many people,
          when, and roughly what you want to spend. She'll come back with a real
          number.
        </p>
        <p class="direct">
          Rather talk? Call or text
          <a href={`tel:${site.phone.replace(/[^\d+]/g, '')}`}>{site.phone}</a>,
          or email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div><PartyQuiz /></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem) clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem); }

  .drivers {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
    margin: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 62rem;
  }

  .drivers li {
    counter-increment: step;
    position: relative;
    padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem 1.15rem 3.6rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .drivers li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    position: absolute;
    left: 1.15rem;
    top: 1.1rem;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--navy-deep);
    background: var(--lemon);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .drivers h3 { font-size: var(--step-0); margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .drivers p { margin: 0; font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--text-muted); }

  .faq {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 280px), 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .faq h3 { font-size: var(--step-1); margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .faq p { margin: 0; font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--text-muted); }

  .band {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .direct { font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--text-muted); }
  .direct a { color: var(--orange); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
  .direct a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .band { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
